+/**
+ * {@link JoinPolicy#AWAIT_ALL}: the scope's outcome is decided when every member has settled, while
+ * deadline, {@code cancelOn}, and parent cancellation still cancel exactly as under fail-fast.
+ *
+ * <p>Invariants and the interleavings each test pins:
+ *
+ * <ul>
+ *   <li>An {@code AWAIT_ALL} token commits {@code COMPLETED} exactly when every bound future has
+ *       settled, whatever they settled as, and a member's failure or cancellation commits nothing.
+ *   <li>A member cancelled directly and a sibling that fails afterwards keep their own
+ *       terminations; the scope is {@code FAILED} by the first failure in declaration order.
+ *   <li>A deadline that fires after a member failed cancels only the unfinished members; finished
+ *       members keep their results and the recorded failure still names the scope.
+ *   <li>A declared combine is cancelled, with a committed {@code ABORTED_BY_FAIL_FAST} reason, by
+ *       the thread that settles the last member when any member did not succeed, before the
+ *       convergence barrier can count it; convergence does not wait for a combine nothing would
+ *       ever settle. The same holds for {@code mapAndCombine}.
+ *   <li>An enclosing scope's cancellation still cancels an {@code AWAIT_ALL} child; a completed
+ *       {@code AWAIT_ALL} token does not cancel its children.
+ *   <li>The sliding window keeps refilling after an element fails.
+ * </ul>
+ */
+@Timeout(value = 60, threadMode = Timeout.ThreadMode.SEPARATE_THREAD)
+@SuppressWarnings("NullAway.Init")
+class AwaitAllJoinPolicyTest {
